\rules only bold italic

A NARROWED RULE SET CHANGES WHAT EVERY LINE BELOW IT MEANS, and no TextMate grammar can follow it: a
rule stack carries regions, never the parser's own rule table. The host stands only bold and italic
here, so ''this bold run'' and //this italic run// build elements and everything else reads as text.

! This heading builds nothing — the host reads the marker as two characters of a paragraph.

* This list marker reads as text too, and so does the `code span` markup around these words.

[[A pretty link]] reads as text. So does <<aMacro>> and {{ATransclusion}}.
